(18-A) "livestock" means farm animals and includes buffaloes, bulls, bullocks, camels, cows, donkeys, goats, sheep,
horses, mules, yaks, pigs, ducks, geese, poultry and their young but does not include any animal specified in [Schedules
I, II and IV];
(19)
"manufacturer" means a person who manufactures articles from any animal or plant specified in [Schedules I, II and III],
as the case may be;
(20)
"meat" includes blood, bones, sinew, eggs, shell or carapace, fat and flesh with or without skin, whether raw or cooked,
of any wild animal or captive animal, other than a vermin;
